WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
- You doing, what are you
doing to fill your time?

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.350
- This is it, I just beg
people to be on their show,

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.713
because I have nothing,
we are in lockdown.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:10.780
No, my kids are obviously, I have

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:11.850
a senior in high school,

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.050
and a sophomore in high school,

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.650
and so they're home,
they're homeschooling,

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.647
and it's--
- Oh, I'm sorry

00:00:16.647 --> 00:00:19.890
for your senior, 'cause this
is like graduation year.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:20.930
- Yeah, it's a tough beat.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.350
I mean, you know, he has a girlfriend,

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.810
so they had prom canceled.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:25.940
They did a little prom thing

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.150
in their backyard the other day,

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.610
just to try and make something special,

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.910
but spring break and prom, and graduation,

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.760
and he plays spring sports.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.560
That was canceled, and so yeah,

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.130
it's a tough way to go out.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.760
- But this is actually,
this is an amazing thing

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.500
'cause I was just actually
speaking with The Voice

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.300
about how long they've
been on or whatever.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.530
And Blake has been there forever,

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.750
but you've been with the Bachelor.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.189
That's 18 years, is that what
- Yeah

00:00:50.189 --> 00:00:51.640
- 18 years--
- That's right

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.380
That's your kid, that's your,

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.850
that's your kid going to college,

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.710
like that's, that's amazing.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.270
Like are, do you feel
like you're a relationship

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:00.900
expert at this point, is my,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.280
'cause I feel like you're probably

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.230
really good at a
relationship how you speak.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.920
- Well it's funny how you
put that in perspective

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.790
because so, my son was six weeks old

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:10.020
when I got the job and so
when he shows up on set

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.440
now he's six foot two
and a big college kid,

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.750
and everyone's like oh
my gosh, that's how long

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.350
we've been doing this
show, it's horrifying.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:18.910
But it is, you know, how long you've been

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:21.420
doing the show, the show's
going to college now.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.200
But I feel like, you
know, I am not a doctor,

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.850
but I definitely should have some sort

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.913
of honorary degree in phycology

00:01:27.913 --> 00:01:28.940
(laughs)

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.490
of dealing with relationships

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.060
'cause I have truly seen it all

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:35.150
and I've been through it
myself and seen it on TV.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.940
- Yeah, of all the people
you've had on this show,

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:40.027
who have you wanted to scream at most

00:01:40.027 --> 00:01:42.421
(laughs loudly)

00:01:42.421 --> 00:01:43.330
- Well it'd be
- Who have you been like

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.449
look you need to take a minute

00:01:45.449 --> 00:01:46.810
(laughs)

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.500
- Gosh, I don't know
if there's anyone who's

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.520
ever been on the show I
haven't wanted to do that.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.500
I mean, even this last season with Peter

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.830
I wanted to just grab
him by the shirt collar

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:59.290
and be like, "Come on
man, pull it together".

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:01.160
'Cause he was a mess
coming down the stretch,

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.010
and Colton obviously jumping the fence

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:03.940
and running away from me in

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.590
the Portuguese countryside.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.910
So yeah, and even Hannah
and I had our moments,

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:10.060
so I think with probably every
- So much drama.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.560
- Probably with every
Bachelor and Bachelorette

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.240
there is that moment where they want

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:15.395
to scream at me, and sometimes they do.

00:02:15.395 --> 00:02:17.470
And I want to yell at them, but that's,

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.010
that's part of, honestly I do get involved

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.310
in these people's lives
and I do care about them.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.360
And I think when you do love people,

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.250
it's not that you abuse
them, that's not love,

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.420
but I think you do have
those heated moments

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:31.240
where you're really telling your truth.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:32.750
- Yeah, I think if you don't, if you don't

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.740
care about someone then
you don't, you don't care

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:35.573
about telling the truth.

00:02:35.573 --> 00:02:36.406
You're just like whatever,

00:02:36.406 --> 00:02:37.490
I'm just going to move along.
- Exactly, yeah.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.440
- Yeah, I think it means something

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.860
when you do get heated, that means that

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.153
you're involved, you're invested.

